# A BMC that answers Get SEL Time but rejects Set SEL Time.
# 
# `sel time set now' reads the host clock, which no snapshot can pin, so this
# transcript uses the neighbouring string instead: strcasecmp() returns a
# non-zero value for "nox" and the argument has to fall through to strptime(),
# which cannot parse it.  "nox" makes strcasecmp() return a positive value and
# "nov" a negative one, so a comparison against any single value other than zero
# would take the "now" branch for one of them.

default_ccode 0xc1

respond get_device_id
  netfn 0x06
  cmd 0x01
  data 20 81 02 03 02 bf 57 01 00 01 00 00 00 00 00
end

respond get_sel_time
  netfn 0x0a
  cmd 0x48
  data 00 e3 0b 5e
end
